// What every service of the commerce engine shares.
//
// The engine answers only the gateway. Every call carries, in its metadata:
//   x-request-id   born in the site or the console; it travels through the
//                  gateway and the engine to the audit log (business book §11.1)
//   x-actor        the person acting, taken from the gateway's session and
//                  never from a field a browser filled (§7.4)
//   x-actor-role   the role they act in
//   authorization  "Bearer <internal token>", shared by gateway and engine
//
// A business refusal (the author signing their own version, a stale version,
// a price under the floor that nobody may approve) is an answer: the response
// carries it as a Refusal, typed. gRPC errors are kept for what is not an
// answer: an unauthenticated call, an unknown id, an engine that broke.

